            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes this is very LSP specific (as it is in `vim/lsp/_watchfiles.lua`), and resolves a severe (and previously misdiagnosed) problem I had with pyright which kept re-registering the same watcher. This caused previous watchers to be closed which (for things like `.venv`) turns out to be very expensive on MacOS. It is still slow to close a server because of this, but starting a server is now down to millisecond range.\r\n\r\nFor context, I'm trying to improve the watchers (by leaning heavily on AI), so we can re-enable them by default on Linux. There won't be a perfect solution, but AI was able to quickly diagnose and fix the bottlenecks which I had previously failed to do so.\r\n\r\n`compile_watchers` can be made more generic and would require internal API changes to `_watch.lua`, but certainly a worthwhile improvement. The main problem is that for this to work we need to be able to compare patterns (globs). `_watch.lua` only deals with LPEG objects which can't be compared, so it would need to have to support LSP-globs directly.",
